  "_comment": "Single source of truth for transcription model download/load metadata. Consumed by the Rust transcription-engine crate (compiled in via include_str!) and the frontend (src/lib/models.ts). To add a model hosted on Hugging Face, add an entry here. Files are listed as a plain string (downloaded by repo path, name kept) or { path, dest } (downloaded then flattened/renamed).",
  "_ui_comment": "The `ui` block drives the model picker, and the picker's ordering is derived from it entirely — there is no hand-maintained sort order anywhere. `accuracy` and `speed` are 1-5 (5 = best); they are the two meters shown per row. `ramMb` is peak memory at load and is a hard constraint, not a preference — a machine below it cannot run the model. `bestFor` lists the languages this model is a *proven strong* choice for, and it promotes the model within its accuracy tier. Omit `bestFor` to derive it from `languageSupport` (a restricted/single-language model is trained on exactly those languages, so its whole set qualifies); set it explicitly to narrow that default, as gigaam-multilingual does to drop `en`. An empty or absent list on a multilingual model means 'unproven, use as fallback' — that is what floats omni-asr to the top for languages nothing else covers well.",
